   "date": "2013-07-21T11:28:34Z",
   "subject": "Basic string manipulation",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi, <br>I am looking for the &quot;R&quot; equivalent of sscanf.<br>Basically I something which looks like this: XXX_3_YYY_4 and I want to extract the 3 and 4 while making sure the pattern holds (i.e. ZZZ_4_AAA_5 would not be legal).<br>The usage would be something like:<br><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:15px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span style=\"color:blue\">a&lt;-c(&quot;XXX_3_YYY_4&quot;, &quot;XXX_26_YYY_12&quot;, &quot;AAA_34_YYY_15&quot;);<br>b&lt;-somefunc(params)<br>&gt;b<br></span></pre></span><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:15px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\">[[1]]\r\n[1] 3 4\r\n\r\n[[2]]\r\n[1] 26 12\r\n\r\n[[3]]\r\n[1] NA<br><br><br><br></pre></span><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:15px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"></span>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "k3Asp6RoS7QJ",
   "from": "Yizhar Toren",
   "author": "a46587f294177886",
   "date": "2013-07-21T11:59:23Z",
   "subject": "Re: [Israel RUG] Basic string manipulation",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Quick and dirty - use two steps:<div><br></div><div>1. use regular expression to validate your expressions:</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">x &lt;- sapply(a, grep, pattern = &#39;^XXX_[0-9]{1,2}_YYY_[0-9]{1,2}$&#39;, value = TRUE)</span><br>\r\n\r\n</div><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">a.filter &lt;- a %in% unlist(x)</span><br></div><div><br></div><div>2. extract what you want:<br></div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">params &lt;- do.call(&#39;rbind&#39;, strsplit(a, split = &#39;_&#39;))</font><br>\r\n\r\n</div><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">params[!a.filter] &lt;- NA</span><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">params[,c(2,4)]</font><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br>\r\n\r\n</font></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Sun, Jul 21, 2013 at 2:28 PM, Assaf Mendelson <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">assaf.m...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n\r\n</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">Hi, <br>I am looking for the &quot;R&quot; equivalent of sscanf.<br>Basically I something which looks like this: XXX_3_YYY_4 and I want to extract the 3 and 4 while making sure the pattern holds (i.e. ZZZ_4_AAA_5 would not be legal).<br>\r\n\r\nThe usage would be something like:<br><span style=\"text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;font-variant:normal;text-align:-webkit-left;font-style:normal;background-color:rgb(225,226,229);font-weight:normal;line-height:15px;border-collapse:separate;text-transform:none;font-size:13px;white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;word-spacing:0px\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:blue\">a&lt;-c(&quot;XXX_3_YYY_4&quot;, &quot;XXX_26_YYY_12&quot;, &quot;AAA_34_YYY_15&quot;);<br>b&lt;-somefunc(params)<br>&gt;b<br></span></pre></span><span style=\"text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;font-variant:normal;text-align:-webkit-left;font-style:normal;background-color:rgb(225,226,229);font-weight:normal;line-height:15px;border-collapse:separate;text-transform:none;font-size:13px;white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;word-spacing:0px\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\">\r\n\r\n[[1]]\r\n[1] 3 4\r\n\r\n[[2]]\r\n[1] 26 12\r\n\r\n[[3]]\r\n[1] NA<span><font color=\"#888888\"><br><br><br><br></font></span></pre></span></blockquote></div></div>"
